    "q-139574": {
      "dom_id": "step-q139574",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "| $x$ | **$-6$** | **$-4$** | **$-2$** | **$0$** | **$2$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $5$ | $8$ | $11$ | $15$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients  of the line $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above can be found using linear regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the design matrix $X$ in this context?",
      "worked_solution": "| $x$ | **$-6$** | **$-4$** | **$-2$** | **$0$** | **$2$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $5$ | $8$ | $11$ | $15$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -6 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 11 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
